{"author":{"id":"5698b6d16d951325374257d86a2e673da0e55970c3d21c0f7c6f49018f24e5bf"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1787157153,"nonce":"cRERde2hVrBkmubbopcIrqi4i88=","message":"**Stage-4 prerequisite audit. One of the three is now clear, one is smaller than it looks, and one is much bigger — it decides whether oto broadcasts at all.**\n\n**Prerequisite 3 is CLEARED.** `bd0fb1d` landed as `4f5204f`: the unacked reminder and its once-per-generation latch at `reminders.go:114-127` are gone root and branch. Comment #5 required this before stage 4, and it is done.\n\n⭐ **And stage 7's hardest clause has DISSOLVED, which is worth knowing before anyone budgets for it.** The body says this ticket *\"reads as reopening a CUT\"* until the distinction between a configurable **identity** and a configurable **delivery-time collapse key** is written into §C.4 and into an ADR superseding 0038. That obligation came from stage 2 — `notification_policies.group_by` plus `Policy.CollapseKey`. **Stage 2 is reverted** (`b70c843`/`ec9dee4`, migration `00065`), and under the one-Case ruling it is not coming back. So no configurable collapse key is being added, and nothing here reopens §C.3's cut of the grouping-rule engine. If anything, deleting the entity **strengthens** *\"Still fixed, still not a rule engine\"* — there is no longer a key to make configurable.\n\n§C.4 still needs a factual edit, because its axes will stop describing a stored entity. But that is recording a deletion, not arguing against a recorded ruling — a completely different weight of work, and it does not need an ADR that supersedes 0038.\n\n⛔ **Prerequisite (b) is NOT independent of (a). It collapses into it, so stage 4 has ONE blocker, not two.** Comment #5 frames (b) as three readers using `notifications.group_id` for subject-shaped questions, implying they can be re-pointed at the `(subject_kind, subject_id)` pair that has existed since `00056`. They cannot. Read the first one:\n\n```sql\n-- internal/notification/repository/rollup.go:100-110\n($3 = 'alert' AND (\n     n.alert_id = $2\n  OR n.group_id IN (SELECT o.group_id FROM alert_cases o\n                     WHERE o.org_id = $1 AND o.alert_id = $2\n                       AND o.group_id IS NOT NULL)))\n```\n\nThat second leg is not a mis-typed subject lookup. It encodes a **fan-out rule**: *a notification about the group counts as a notification about each member alert*. Once a conversation is a Case, there is no container for that rule to be about — so the leg is **deleted, not re-pointed**, and the `$3 = 'alert_group'` arm goes with it. Whether that is right depends entirely on whether group-scoped notifications still exist, which is (a). Same for the audit filter and for the drill reads.\n\n⚠️ **And the drill subsystem is a fourth consumer the \"three readers\" framing undercounts.** It does not merely read `group_id`, it JOINs the table: `internal/drill/repository/artifacts.go:200` `JOIN alert_groups g ON g.id = o.group_id AND g.org_id = o.org_id`, plus `:243` `WHERE n.org_id = $1 AND n.group_id = $2`, and `dispose.go:80` and `:125`. `internal/drill/domain/stage.go:33` names its evidence as *\"`alert_groups`, `alert_cases.group_id`\"*. Stage 4 has to answer what a drill's evidence becomes, and that is not in the ticket.\n\n\n`BroadcastPolicy.Warrants` (`internal/notification/domain/broadcast.go:99-108`) returns true for exactly two Reasons:\n\n```go\ncase ReasonRefired:     return true\ncase ReasonAllResolved: return p.Resolved\n```\n\nAnd **`refired` has no producer.** `git grep -nI 'ReasonRefired' -- '*.go'` outside tests returns eight lines, all vocabulary, classification or rendering; `alerts/service/service.go`'s `reasonFor(TransitionID)` has no T8 case and `TransitionT8` does not exist outside tests; `broadcast.go:71` says it itself — *\"⛔ RETAINED FOR HISTORY; NOTHING PRODUCES IT.\"* ADR 0040 retired T8.\n\nSo `all_resolved` is the only member of that set anything can reach. **If it dies with `alert_groups`, `Warrants` can never return true again** — `ModeBroadcastReply` becomes unreachable, `MsgOptionBroadcast()` at `providers/slack/channel.go:87` becomes dead, `broadcast_on_resolved` becomes a setting that governs nothing, ADR 0020 in its entirety becomes a document about a mechanism oto does not use, and the affordance just landed for `68653ca` (`17f8055`, plus ADR 0020 Amendment 5) becomes dead code the week it shipped.\n\nThat is not an argument for either answer. It is the consequence that was not connected to the question, and it makes (a) a product decision about **broadcast**, not a plumbing decision about two Reasons.\n\n**The two coherent answers, and what each costs:**\n\n- **Both Reasons die with the container.** Honest and consistent with the ruling — they describe a cardinality that no longer exists, exactly as `group_by`/`CollapseKey` did. Cost: broadcast dies too, and everything above goes with it. If this is the answer, `refired` should also leave the Reason vocabulary in the same migration rather than lingering as history, and ADR 0020 needs a supersession note saying oto no longer surfaces anything in a channel.\n- **`new_alerts` dies; `all_resolved` collapses into the Case's own resolve.** A Case resolving is a fact about the Case, lands in the Case's conversation, stays broadcastable. Broadcast survives, `broadcast_on_resolved` keeps meaning, and the set becomes one real Reason instead of one real plus one dormant. Cost: `all_resolved` is a *rename* with a migration on `notifications_reason_ck`, and the render arm at `reply.go:149-159` and its \"N of M instances\" clause lose their object — a Case has no instance count.\n\n⭐ The second reading also removes a standing oddity: today's broadcast set is one Reason nothing produces plus one that is default-off, so **oto broadcasts nothing out of the box**. Under it the set becomes one reachable Reason, which is the first time `reply_broadcast` would mean something in practice.\n\n\nNo code. Stage 4 is *\"the largest and least reversible remaining stage\"* (961 occurrences / 175 files / 38 OpenAPI sites, this ticket's own measurement), its single remaining blocker is a product decision with the consequences above, and (b) turned out not to be separable from it — so there is no independent slice to land first. Building either answer to (a) unattended would be building the wrong thing correctly, which is what the handoff §4 records as this project's most expensive failure mode.\n\n**The one question:** does `all_resolved` survive as a fact about the Case, or does broadcast go with `alert_groups`?","files":null}]}